-- BREACH-PLAYBOOKS-TOOL-LOOP-1 (2026-10-26, charter pillar autonomy; agent_issues 1000266 BREACH-DOCTOR-1, package tool-loop-playbooks).
-- The breach doctor (qnfo-fleet-control 0.52.0, migrations/2026-10-26-breach-doctor.sql) diagnosed 40 issues on its first tick and could remediate none of the tool, loop, secret and
-- owner-request families, because only the four CODE-MERGE-REFUSED-1 / CODE-LOOP-EXHAUSTED-1 seed rules existed. This file adds the playbook rows for those families. A playbook is data: the
-- engine validates every statement (one read-only SELECT per trigger and verify, one INSERT or UPDATE on an allowlisted table per action and revert, bound to ?1 = the issue, no free-text column)
-- and holds a new row in measure for 30 minutes; a rule with 2 failed cases in 24 hours demotes itself. The engine changes are in qnfo-fleet-control 0.54.0: tool_error_exclusions joins BD_WRITE_TABLES (the
-- allowlist of tables a playbook may write); a verify_sql that reads pending-<reason> keeps an applied case waiting for an effect another loop produces (PENDING-VERIFY-1); the owner card of the owner-card
-- kind carries an empty default_in_effect, and a handed-owner case verifies only on a card the owner resolved.
-- REVIEW 2026-10-26 (nine blocking findings of the package reviewers, each reproduced on a scratch fixture before it was fixed):
--   TL-R12-owner-card is REMOVED. (1) The live trigger human_actions_default_adopt_ai closed the engine's card at birth (status resolved, DEFAULT-ADOPTED-1) because the card was not decision-shaped, so the owner never saw it and
--   the case verified on any non-open status: fixed in the engine (empty default_in_effect, verify only on a card the owner resolved) and tested against the live trigger, views and markers. (2) The card said the fleet had not worked
--   around the blocker while nothing was attempted and no blocker_redteam row existed (doctrine section 3); the one task it served, 100488, asks the fleet to propose the smallest concrete step and log it for owner approval, which is
--   the fleet's own step. A rule of the owner-card kind returns with its blocker_redteam row in its own migration.
--   TL-R09-paper-route is REMOVED, and goals and paper_learnings are not on the allowlist. Nothing in worker code or a D1 trigger moves an instrumental goal from proposed to adopted (the only adopting code is the dashboard's step for a ratified
--   objective revision; 7 instrumental goals proposed on 2026-10-19/20 were untouched on 2026-10-26, live D1 read), so the rule
--   moved the PL-TRIAGE-1 apply rows to a sink nobody reads and let the PAPER-LEARN-1 contracts pass without a doer; its reject half applied a bar PL-TRIAGE-1 never used (confidence under 0.7, or an assumption: PL-TRIAGE-1 rejects only
--   with two model families agreeing); a row failing a slug, version or kind guard (95 of the 1,173 proposed direct learnings carry a version such as v0.3, live D1 read) was neither routed nor rejected and failed the case. PAPER-LEARN-1 stays with qnfo-lifecycle PL-TRIAGE-1 and the
--   issues' own contracts until a loop that consumes the rows exists.
--   TL-R07-secret ships in MEASURE: its evidence measures one clause of the three-clause definition of done of a security issue and said 'verified'. It records the case and closes nothing (control breach-doctor-secret-change-measure).
--   TL-R03-exclude: four of the 20 literals belong to several tools, tool_error_exclusions.pattern is its primary key, and the second case of a shared literal in one tick inserted nothing and failed no-rows. The trigger now names
--   only the tool of the lowest issue id among the eligible tools that share an absent literal; the others follow one tick later with the literals of their own, or are closed by TL-R03-close once the shared literal classes their
--   errors. Verify reads the outcome (every reviewed literal of the tool is excluded), not who wrote it. The table gets a nullable issue_id column (the id of the issue whose case added the row) because the structural gate of
--   0.53.1 (BREACH-DOCTOR-GATE-1, merged while this package was in review) refuses an INSERT that fills no issue_id and an UPDATE ... FROM; the revert is now bound by issue_id = ?1. No ON CONFLICT clause is used, so the
--   statements also pass the stricter gate of PR 4599 (a clause keyed by anything but issue_id needs its own WHERE issue_id = ?1, which a no-op upsert of a shared literal cannot have).
--   TL-R01-rearm: verify read the marker the action wrote, so every case verified without the planner reading anything, and the trigger fired while the planner was at its daily cap (48 of 48). It is gated on planner capacity and verifies
--   on the planner re-recording the issue with a verdict other than untrusted.
-- Trigger hit counts measured on live qnfo-audit 2026-10-26 11:55Z (SELECT only, each trigger run as the engine runs it): TL-R01-rearm 28 before the capacity gate and 0 with it (the planner is at its cap: 48 of 48 model plans at 01:47Z); TL-R03-exclude 1 (git_op 1000405; fleet_graph 100436 was a second hit an hour earlier, until its errors left the 24-hour window); TL-R03-close 1 (TOOL-ERROR-RATE ops_d1_query 1000023, all 6 errors of 24 hours classed); TL-R05-dedupe 2 (SELF-AUDIT-TOOLERR 1000052 into 100436, 1000381 into 1000312);
-- TL-R07-secret 4 (100333 qnfo-ops, 100418 qnfo-research-exec, 1000199 qnfo-ai-search, 1000200 qnfo-fleet-dashboard; recorded in measure, none closed); TL-R12-owner-dup 0 (a session closed the 18 duplicates of the audit; the rule keeps the dashboard buttons from refilling them).
-- Rules (every one: a trigger that names exactly the issues, an action bound to one issue, a revert, a verify that reads a reason before and ok after, close_evidence built from ids, counts and enum codes):
--   TL-R01-rearm        issue_plans.planned_at to 2000-01-01 for an untrusted verdict the trust list now covers while the planner has capacity (the planner re-reads it on its next tick; verified when it has)
--   TL-R03-exclude      insert of a tool's reviewed error literals into tool_error_exclusions (20 literals, each emitted by the owning worker or D1), one case per tool, behind a surge guard; a tool that shares an absent literal with a lower-id eligible tool waits a tick
--   TL-R03-close        close a tool issue with counts when no unexcluded error of its tool remains in 24 hours (at least 5 calls, one ok, no surge, no failing contract)
--   TL-R05-dedupe       supersede the duplicate signals of one tool (TOOL-FAILURE, TOOL-ERROR-RATE, SELF-AUDIT-TOOLERR, [self-heal]) into the TOOL-FAILURE row
--   TL-R07-secret       MEASURE: record SECRET-CHANGE-OBSERVED when the worker is registered, deployed and in sync after the change and shows no 401 or 403 in 2 hours (read only, no secret read); closes nothing
--   TL-R12-owner-dup    supersede exact duplicates of a dashboard-generated OWNER-TASK prompt into the lowest id
-- Two code levers are seeded as issues, because the doctor edits no code (one anchored edit in one file each, verified byte-exact and unique on origin/main 2026-10-26, outcome probe in the issue's contract):
--   BREACH-DOCTOR-1: TD-D1Q-REJECT qnfo-ops               anchor 'const out = { ok: false, db: bind, error: msg };' occurs 1 time in qnfo-ops/worker.js (d1Query lacks the D1-CALLER-REJECT-1 treatment d1Write has)
--   BREACH-DOCTOR-1: R2-PLAN-FIRST qnfo-code-orchestrator anchor 'const ord = " ORDER BY CASE a.priority ... a.id LIMIT ";' occurs 1 time in qnfo-code-orchestrator/worker.js (first-time plans before re-plans)
-- Left out, with the reason (see the decision_log row): R6 chaos drills (probe repoints already landed in migrations/2026-10-26-chaos-drill-calibration.sql and 2026-10-26-sweep-probe-fixes-b.sql, the rest
-- wait for research-exec recovery), TD-EMPTY-ERROR (git_clone_exec and shell_pipeline: 5 and 6 errors in 7 days, so no outcome probe can fail until traffic returns), R11 stub workers (the registry writer is not one anchored edit), R8 cf-changelog (the check is a source search outside D1), R10 workflow-failed (no stored fact of the workflow files on main; the live issue is a real failing run),
-- R9 paper-route and R12 owner-card (removed in review, see above), R12b moot (0 live hits), R13 loop-breaker (both rows self-close six hours after the last recurrence, about 12:07Z), TL-14 (unproven).
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE breach_playbooks SET enabled = 0, mode = 'measure' WHERE rule_id LIKE 'TL-R%'; UPDATE tool_error_exclusions SET pattern = 'TOOL-CLASSIFY-2-REVERTED ' || pattern, rationale = 'REVERTED ' || rationale WHERE instr(rationale, 'TOOL-CLASSIFY-2 ') = 1 AND instr(pattern, 'TOOL-CLASSIFY-2-REVERTED ') <> 1; DELETE FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class IN ('fm-tool-exclusion-hides-outage', 'fm-stale-untrusted-verdict'); DELETE FROM failure_modes WHERE fm_key IN ('tool-exclusion-hides-outage', 'stale-untrusted-verdict'); DELETE FROM control_registry WHERE control IN ('breach-doctor-tool-exclusion-rule', 'breach-doctor-secret-change-measure'); UPDATE control_registry SET location = replace(location, 'one INSERT or UPDATE on five named tables (issue_triage, agent_issues UPDATE only, remediation_contracts, issue_plans, tool_error_exclusions)', 'one INSERT or UPDATE on four named tables (issue_triage, agent_issues UPDATE only, remediation_contracts, issue_plans)') WHERE control = 'breach-doctor-action-allowlist'; DELETE FROM capability_ledger WHERE capability = 'breach-doctor:tool-loop-playbooks'; the engine keeps its ledger, the nullable tool_error_exclusions.issue_id column stays (unread), decision_log is append-only and stays, and the two seeded code-lever issues stay open (an issue is closed only with close_evidence)
-- spof-review: no new cron, worker, binding or credential. Net-zero rule: no table family is added (the rows are data in breach_playbooks).

-- tool_error_exclusions gets the id of the issue whose case added a row (nullable, unread by every other reader): the structural id-bound check of qnfo-fleet-control 0.53.1 (BREACH-DOCTOR-GATE-1) accepts an INSERT
-- only when it fills an issue_id column from the bound issue, and an UPDATE only with a top-level issue_id = ?1 predicate, so a table with no such column could not be written by a playbook at all. The runner
-- tolerates a second apply (duplicate column name, scripts/apply_migrations.py).
ALTER TABLE tool_error_exclusions ADD COLUMN issue_id INTEGER;

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO breach_playbooks (rule_id, version, family, cause_class, action_kind, trigger_sql, action_sql, revert_sql, verify_sql, min_ladder, max_per_tick, max_per_day, enabled, mode, note) VALUES
  ('TL-R01-rearm', 1, '*', 'stale-untrusted-verdict', 'sql', 'WITH RECURSIVE cfg(v) AS (SELECT value || '','' FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''code_merge_trusted_sources''), split(entry, rest) AS (SELECT '''', v FROM cfg UNION ALL SELECT trim(substr(rest, 1, instr(rest, '','') - 1)), substr(rest, instr(rest, '','') + 1) FROM split WHERE rest <> ''''), rules AS (SELECT CASE WHEN instr(entry, ''|'') > 0 THEN substr(entry, 1, instr(entry, ''|'') - 1) ELSE entry END AS sp, CASE WHEN instr(entry, ''|'') > 0 THEN substr(entry, instr(entry, ''|'') + 1) ELSE '''' END AS tp FROM split WHERE entry <> '''') SELECT a.id AS issue_id, ''stale-untrusted'' AS subject, json_object(''plan_age_h'', CAST((julianday(''now'') - julianday(p.planned_at)) * 24 AS INTEGER), ''planned_at_was'', p.planned_at, ''attempts'', COALESCE(p.attempts, 1)) AS facts_json FROM issue_plans p JOIN agent_issues a ON a.id = p.issue_id WHERE a.status = ''open'' AND p.outcome = ''untrusted'' AND p.planned_at > ''2001-01-01T00:00:00Z'' AND a.title NOT LIKE ''BREACH-DOCTOR-1:%'' AND p.planned_at >= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'',''-7 days'') AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM rules r WHERE r.sp <> '''' AND r.sp <> ''*'' AND (CASE WHEN substr(r.sp, -1) = ''*'' THEN substr(COALESCE(a.source, ''''), 1, length(r.sp) - 1) = substr(r.sp, 1, length(r.sp) - 1) ELSE COALESCE(a.source, '''') = r.sp END) AND (r.tp = '''' OR substr(COALESCE(a.title, ''''), 1, length(r.tp)) = r.tp)) AND (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM issue_plans q WHERE q.planned_at >= strftime(''%Y-%m-%d'', ''now'') AND q.model IS NOT NULL) < COALESCE((SELECT MIN(200, MAX(1, CAST(c.value AS INTEGER))) FROM ops_config c WHERE c.key = ''code_plan_daily_cap'' AND c.value GLOB ''[0-9]*''), 24) ORDER BY CASE a.priority WHEN ''critical'' THEN 0 WHEN ''high'' THEN 1 WHEN ''medium'' THEN 2 ELSE 3 END, a.id LIMIT MAX(0, 6 - (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM breach_diagnoses f WHERE f.rule_id = ''TL-R01-rearm'' AND f.state IN (''queued'', ''applied'', ''verifying'')))',
   json_array('UPDATE issue_plans SET planned_at = ''2000-01-01T00:00:00Z'' WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND outcome = ''untrusted'' AND planned_at > ''2001-01-01T00:00:00Z'''),
   json_array('UPDATE issue_plans SET planned_at = strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ'',''now'') WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND outcome = ''untrusted'' AND planned_at = ''2000-01-01T00:00:00Z'''),
   'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_plans WHERE issue_id = ?1) THEN ''plan-row-missing'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_plans WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND planned_at < ''2001-01-01T00:00:00Z'') THEN ''pending-planner-reread'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_plans WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND outcome = ''untrusted'') THEN ''still-stale-untrusted'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed', 'delegated', 6, 40, 1, 'on', 'An open issue whose planner verdict is untrusted although its (source, title) now matches ops_config code_merge_trusted_sources by the planner''s own grammar (entry, entry*, entry|title-prefix): the list grew on 2026-10-24 and the planner re-reads a non-queued verdict only after 7 days (PLAN_RECHECK_DAYS). Action: issue_plans.planned_at to 2000-01-01 so the next planner tick re-reads it (precedent migrations/2026-10-20-plan-trust-parity.sql); the old value is in the case facts (planned_at_was) and revert_sql restarts the 7-day timer. The planner''s deny list and merge scope still apply at plan time. REVIEW 2026-10-26 (the marker was its own proof): verify no longer reads the marker the action wrote. It reads pending-planner-reread while the marker stands (the engine waits for it until the case lease ends, then lease-expired, PENDING-VERIFY-1), still-stale-untrusted when the planner re-recorded the issue and it is still untrusted (the rule''s belief that the list covers it was wrong: the case fails and the rule demotes itself), and ok only when the planner has re-recorded the issue with a verdict other than untrusted. Capacity: the trigger names nothing while the planner has no model call left today (issue_plans rows with a model since 00:00Z against ops_config code_plan_daily_cap, default 24; planIssues returns daily cap before it reads a row, 48 of 48 at 01:47Z on 2026-10-26, so a marker would sit unread until 00:00Z), and it names at most 6 minus the TL-R01 cases in flight, highest priority first, so the markers outstanding never exceed what the planner (every 2 minutes, one model call and up to 10 recordings a tick) takes in one lease. Live 2026-10-26: 28 hits before the capacity gate. Priority order among first-time plans is R2-PLAN-FIRST, seeded below. The trigger skips a row already at the marker, so the rule cannot loop.');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO breach_playbooks (rule_id, version, family, cause_class, action_kind, trigger_sql, action_sql, revert_sql, verify_sql, min_ladder, max_per_tick, max_per_day, enabled, mode, note) VALUES
  ('TL-R03-close', 1, 'TOOL-FAILURE', 'tool-errors-all-classed', 'sql', 'WITH r(rule_key, tool, pat, cls) AS (VALUES (''fg-find'', ''fleet_graph'', ''use fleet_graph_find'', ''agent-input-error''), (''gh404-issue-get'', ''github_issue_get'', ''GitHub 404: Not Found'', ''agent-input-error''), (''gh404-issue-comment'', ''github_issue_comment'', ''GitHub 404: Not Found'', ''agent-input-error''), (''gh404-git-op'', ''git_op'', ''GitHub 404: Not Found'', ''agent-input-error''), (''gh422-git-op'', ''git_op'', ''GitHub 422: No commit found for SHA'', ''agent-input-error''), (''repo-git-op'', ''git_op'', ''repo (owner/name) required'', ''agent-input-error''), (''repo-file-write'', ''github_file_write'', ''repo (owner/name) + path required'', ''agent-input-error''), (''self-fetch'', ''web_fetch'', ''self-fetch blocked'', ''correct-refusal''), (''ctr-timeout-exec'', ''shell_exec'', ''container timeout after'', ''infra-artifact''), (''ctr-timeout-ws'', ''container_workspace_exec'', ''container timeout after'', ''infra-artifact''), (''cfdocs-path'', ''cf_docs'', ''path must be a developers.cloudflare.com path'', ''agent-input-error''), (''cfdocs-page'', ''cf_docs'', ''docs page not found'', ''agent-input-error''), (''cfdocs-query'', ''cf_docs'', ''query required for mode'', ''agent-input-error''), (''netjs-json'', ''run_code_net'', '' is not valid JSON'', ''agent-input-error''), (''netjs-52x'', ''run_code_net'', ''error code: 52'', ''infra-artifact''), (''d1q-syntax'', ''ops_d1_query'', '': syntax error at offset'', ''agent-input-error''), (''d1q-token'', ''ops_d1_query'', ''D1_ERROR: unrecognized token'', ''agent-input-error''), (''d1q-terms'', ''ops_d1_query'', ''too many terms in compound SELECT'', ''agent-input-error''), (''d1w-token'', ''ops_d1_write'', ''D1_ERROR: unrecognized token'', ''agent-input-error''), (''d1w-terms'', ''ops_d1_write'', ''too many terms in compound SELECT'', ''agent-input-error'')), iss AS (SELECT id, CASE WHEN title LIKE ''TOOL-FAILURE: % [error]'' THEN substr(title, 15, length(title) - 22) WHEN title LIKE ''SELF-AUDIT-TOOLERR: %'' THEN substr(title, 21) WHEN title LIKE ''[self-heal] tool % failing%'' THEN substr(title, 18, instr(substr(title, 18), '' '') - 1) WHEN title LIKE ''TOOL-ERROR-RATE-%-1'' THEN substr(title, 17, length(title) - 18) END AS tool, CASE WHEN title LIKE ''TOOL-FAILURE:%'' THEN 0 WHEN title LIKE ''SELF-AUDIT-TOOLERR:%'' THEN 1 WHEN title LIKE ''TOOL-ERROR-RATE-%'' THEN 1 ELSE 2 END AS rk FROM agent_issues WHERE status = ''open'' AND (title LIKE ''TOOL-FAILURE: %'' OR title LIKE ''SELF-AUDIT-TOOLERR: %'' OR title LIKE ''[self-heal] tool %'' OR title LIKE ''TOOL-ERROR-RATE-%-1'')), v AS (SELECT id, tool, rk FROM iss WHERE tool IS NOT NULL AND length(tool) BETWEEN 2 AND 40 AND tool NOT GLOB ''*[^a-z0-9_]*''), st AS (SELECT v.tool AS tool, COUNT(*) AS calls, SUM(CASE WHEN e.status = ''ok'' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS oks, SUM(CASE WHEN e.status = ''error'' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS errs, SUM(CASE WHEN e.status = ''error'' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM tool_error_exclusions x WHERE instr(COALESCE(e.meta,''''), x.pattern) > 0 OR instr(COALESCE(e.text,''''), x.pattern) > 0) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS unexcl, SUM(CASE WHEN e.status = ''error'' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM tool_error_exclusions x WHERE instr(COALESCE(e.meta,''''), x.pattern) > 0 OR instr(COALESCE(e.text,''''), x.pattern) > 0) AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM r WHERE r.tool = v.tool AND instr(COALESCE(e.meta,''''), r.pat) > 0) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS covered, SUM(CASE WHEN e.ts >= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'',''-6 hours'') THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS calls_6h, SUM(CASE WHEN e.ts >= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'',''-6 hours'') AND e.status = ''error'' AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM r WHERE r.tool = v.tool AND instr(COALESCE(e.meta,''''), r.pat) > 0) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS classed_6h FROM (SELECT DISTINCT tool FROM v) v JOIN cloud_ops_events e ON e.kind = ''ops_ai_tool'' AND e.text = v.tool AND e.ts >= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'',''-24 hours'') GROUP BY v.tool) SELECT v.id AS issue_id, v.tool AS subject, json_object(''tool'', v.tool, ''calls_24h'', st.calls, ''errors_24h'', st.errs, ''classed_24h'', st.errs - st.unexcl, ''unexcluded_24h'', st.unexcl) AS facts_json FROM v JOIN st ON st.tool = v.tool JOIN agent_issues a ON a.id = v.id WHERE st.unexcl = 0 AND st.calls >= 5 AND st.oks >= 1 AND NOT (st.calls_6h >= 10 AND st.classed_6h * 100 >= 30 * st.calls_6h) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts fc WHERE fc.issue_id = a.id AND fc.status IN (''active'',''holding'') AND COALESCE(fc.last_verdict,'''') IN (''fail'',''vacuous-probe-result'',''probe-error'',''probe-not-machine-executable'',''probe-same-account-host'')) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM work_claims wc WHERE (wc.issue_id = a.id OR wc.path = ''issue:'' || a.id) AND wc.released_at IS NULL AND wc.expires_at > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now''))',
   json_array('INSERT INTO issue_triage (issue_id, rc, triage_state, owner, sla_due_at, close_evidence) SELECT a.id, ''breach-doctor:TL-R03-close'', ''closed'', ''breach-doctor'', datetime(''now''), ''TOOL-CLASSIFY-2 '' || strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'') || '': tool '' || json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.tool'') || '' made '' || json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.calls_24h'') || '' calls in the last 24 hours with '' || json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.errors_24h'') || '' errors, '' || json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.classed_24h'') || '' of them covered by a reviewed tool_error_exclusions class and '' || json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.unexcluded_24h'') || '' by none, and at least one call succeeded, so no unclassified failure of this tool remains. Closed by breach-doctor rule TL-R03-close from cloud_ops_events counts only (no event text read). Recheck: tool_failures_24h genuine_failures for this tool stays 0, and a new unclassified error files a new TOOL-FAILURE issue.'' FROM agent_issues a JOIN breach_diagnoses d ON d.issue_id = a.id AND d.id = (SELECT MAX(x.id) FROM breach_diagnoses x WHERE x.issue_id = a.id AND x.state IN (''diagnosed'',''queued'')) WHERE a.id = ?1 AND a.status = ''open'' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts fc WHERE fc.issue_id = a.id AND fc.status IN (''active'',''holding'') AND COALESCE(fc.last_verdict,'''') IN (''fail'',''vacuous-probe-result'',''probe-error'',''probe-not-machine-executable'',''probe-same-account-host'')) ON CONFLICT(issue_id) DO UPDATE SET rc = excluded.rc, triage_state = ''closed'', owner = ''breach-doctor'', close_evidence = excluded.close_evidence'),
   json_array('UPDATE issue_triage SET triage_state = ''triaged'', close_evidence = NULL WHERE issue_id = ?1', 'UPDATE agent_issues SET status = ''open'', close_channel = NULL, updated_at = CAST(strftime(''%s'',''now'') AS INTEGER) * 1000 WHERE id = ?1 AND status = ''closed'''),
   'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE id = ?1 AND status IN (''closed'',''resolved'')) THEN ''ok'' ELSE ''issue-reopened'' END AS observed', 'delegated', 6, 30, 1, 'on', 'A TOOL-FAILURE, TOOL-ERROR-RATE, SELF-AUDIT-TOOLERR or [self-heal] issue whose tool has no error in the last 24 hours that tool_error_exclusions does not cover, at least 5 calls and a successful one (silence is not recovery), no 6-hour surge of excluded-class errors (30 percent of at least 10 calls) and no failing active contract (the TOOL-ISSUE-SELFCLOSE-1 probe counts the raw error share, so a failing contract is left to it). Closes with close_evidence made of counts. Live 2026-10-26: the TOOL-ERROR-RATE issue of ops_d1_query (1000023) reaches this at once, the others after TL-R03-exclude.');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO breach_playbooks (rule_id, version, family, cause_class, action_kind, trigger_sql, action_sql, revert_sql, verify_sql, min_ladder, max_per_tick, max_per_day, enabled, mode, note) VALUES
  ('TL-R03-exclude', 1, 'TOOL-FAILURE', 'reviewed-tool-error-class', 'sql', 'WITH r(rule_key, tool, pat, cls) AS (VALUES (''fg-find'', ''fleet_graph'', ''use fleet_graph_find'', ''agent-input-error''), (''gh404-issue-get'', ''github_issue_get'', ''GitHub 404: Not Found'', ''agent-input-error''), (''gh404-issue-comment'', ''github_issue_comment'', ''GitHub 404: Not Found'', ''agent-input-error''), (''gh404-git-op'', ''git_op'', ''GitHub 404: Not Found'', ''agent-input-error''), (''gh422-git-op'', ''git_op'', ''GitHub 422: No commit found for SHA'', ''agent-input-error''), (''repo-git-op'', ''git_op'', ''repo (owner/name) required'', ''agent-input-error''), (''repo-file-write'', ''github_file_write'', ''repo (owner/name) + path required'', ''agent-input-error''), (''self-fetch'', ''web_fetch'', ''self-fetch blocked'', ''correct-refusal''), (''ctr-timeout-exec'', ''shell_exec'', ''container timeout after'', ''infra-artifact''), (''ctr-timeout-ws'', ''container_workspace_exec'', ''container timeout after'', ''infra-artifact''), (''cfdocs-path'', ''cf_docs'', ''path must be a developers.cloudflare.com path'', ''agent-input-error''), (''cfdocs-page'', ''cf_docs'', ''docs page not found'', ''agent-input-error''), (''cfdocs-query'', ''cf_docs'', ''query required for mode'', ''agent-input-error''), (''netjs-json'', ''run_code_net'', '' is not valid JSON'', ''agent-input-error''), (''netjs-52x'', ''run_code_net'', ''error code: 52'', ''infra-artifact''), (''d1q-syntax'', ''ops_d1_query'', '': syntax error at offset'', ''agent-input-error''), (''d1q-token'', ''ops_d1_query'', ''D1_ERROR: unrecognized token'', ''agent-input-error''), (''d1q-terms'', ''ops_d1_query'', ''too many terms in compound SELECT'', ''agent-input-error''), (''d1w-token'', ''ops_d1_write'', ''D1_ERROR: unrecognized token'', ''agent-input-error''), (''d1w-terms'', ''ops_d1_write'', ''too many terms in compound SELECT'', ''agent-input-error'')), iss AS (SELECT id, CASE WHEN title LIKE ''TOOL-FAILURE: % [error]'' THEN substr(title, 15, length(title) - 22) WHEN title LIKE ''SELF-AUDIT-TOOLERR: %'' THEN substr(title, 21) WHEN title LIKE ''[self-heal] tool % failing%'' THEN substr(title, 18, instr(substr(title, 18), '' '') - 1) WHEN title LIKE ''TOOL-ERROR-RATE-%-1'' THEN substr(title, 17, length(title) - 18) END AS tool, CASE WHEN title LIKE ''TOOL-FAILURE:%'' THEN 0 WHEN title LIKE ''SELF-AUDIT-TOOLERR:%'' THEN 1 WHEN title LIKE ''TOOL-ERROR-RATE-%'' THEN 1 ELSE 2 END AS rk FROM agent_issues WHERE status = ''open'' AND (title LIKE ''TOOL-FAILURE: %'' OR title LIKE ''SELF-AUDIT-TOOLERR: %'' OR title LIKE ''[self-heal] tool %'' OR title LIKE ''TOOL-ERROR-RATE-%-1'')), v AS (SELECT id, tool, rk FROM iss WHERE tool IS NOT NULL AND length(tool) BETWEEN 2 AND 40 AND tool NOT GLOB ''*[^a-z0-9_]*''), st AS (SELECT v.tool AS tool, COUNT(*) AS calls, SUM(CASE WHEN e.status = ''ok'' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS oks, SUM(CASE WHEN e.status = ''error'' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS errs, SUM(CASE WHEN e.status = ''error'' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM tool_error_exclusions x WHERE instr(COALESCE(e.meta,''''), x.pattern) > 0 OR instr(COALESCE(e.text,''''), x.pattern) > 0) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS unexcl, SUM(CASE WHEN e.status = ''error'' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM tool_error_exclusions x WHERE instr(COALESCE(e.meta,''''), x.pattern) > 0 OR instr(COALESCE(e.text,''''), x.pattern) > 0) AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM r WHERE r.tool = v.tool AND instr(COALESCE(e.meta,''''), r.pat) > 0) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS covered, SUM(CASE WHEN e.ts >= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'',''-6 hours'') THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS calls_6h, SUM(CASE WHEN e.ts >= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'',''-6 hours'') AND e.status = ''error'' AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM r WHERE r.tool = v.tool AND instr(COALESCE(e.meta,''''), r.pat) > 0) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS classed_6h FROM (SELECT DISTINCT tool FROM v) v JOIN cloud_ops_events e ON e.kind = ''ops_ai_tool'' AND e.text = v.tool AND e.ts >= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'',''-24 hours'') GROUP BY v.tool), el AS (SELECT v.id AS id, v.tool AS tool FROM v JOIN st ON st.tool = v.tool WHERE st.covered > 0 AND NOT (st.calls_6h >= 10 AND st.classed_6h * 100 >= 30 * st.calls_6h) AND v.id = (SELECT MIN(w.id) FROM v w WHERE w.tool = v.tool)) SELECT el.id AS issue_id, el.tool AS subject, json_object(''tool'', el.tool, ''calls_24h'', st.calls, ''errors_24h'', st.errs, ''unexcluded_24h'', st.unexcl, ''covered_24h'', st.covered, ''rules'', (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM r WHERE r.tool = el.tool)) AS facts_json FROM el JOIN st ON st.tool = el.tool WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM el e2 JOIN r r2 ON r2.tool = e2.tool JOIN r r1 ON r1.tool = el.tool AND r1.pat = r2.pat WHERE e2.id < el.id AND e2.tool <> el.tool AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM tool_error_exclusions x WHERE x.pattern = r1.pat))',
   json_array('WITH r(rule_key, tool, pat, cls) AS (VALUES (''fg-find'', ''fleet_graph'', ''use fleet_graph_find'', ''agent-input-error''), (''gh404-issue-get'', ''github_issue_get'', ''GitHub 404: Not Found'', ''agent-input-error''), (''gh404-issue-comment'', ''github_issue_comment'', ''GitHub 404: Not Found'', ''agent-input-error''), (''gh404-git-op'', ''git_op'', ''GitHub 404: Not Found'', ''agent-input-error''), (''gh422-git-op'', ''git_op'', ''GitHub 422: No commit found for SHA'', ''agent-input-error''), (''repo-git-op'', ''git_op'', ''repo (owner/name) required'', ''agent-input-error''), (''repo-file-write'', ''github_file_write'', ''repo (owner/name) + path required'', ''agent-input-error''), (''self-fetch'', ''web_fetch'', ''self-fetch blocked'', ''correct-refusal''), (''ctr-timeout-exec'', ''shell_exec'', ''container timeout after'', ''infra-artifact''), (''ctr-timeout-ws'', ''container_workspace_exec'', ''container timeout after'', ''infra-artifact''), (''cfdocs-path'', ''cf_docs'', ''path must be a developers.cloudflare.com path'', ''agent-input-error''), (''cfdocs-page'', ''cf_docs'', ''docs page not found'', ''agent-input-error''), (''cfdocs-query'', ''cf_docs'', ''query required for mode'', ''agent-input-error''), (''netjs-json'', ''run_code_net'', '' is not valid JSON'', ''agent-input-error''), (''netjs-52x'', ''run_code_net'', ''error code: 52'', ''infra-artifact''), (''d1q-syntax'', ''ops_d1_query'', '': syntax error at offset'', ''agent-input-error''), (''d1q-token'', ''ops_d1_query'', ''D1_ERROR: unrecognized token'', ''agent-input-error''), (''d1q-terms'', ''ops_d1_query'', ''too many terms in compound SELECT'', ''agent-input-error''), (''d1w-token'', ''ops_d1_write'', ''D1_ERROR: unrecognized token'', ''agent-input-error''), (''d1w-terms'', ''ops_d1_write'', ''too many terms in compound SELECT'', ''agent-input-error'')) INSERT OR IGNORE INTO tool_error_exclusions (pattern, err_class, rationale, issue_id) SELECT r.pat, r.cls, ''TOOL-CLASSIFY-2 '' || strftime(''%Y-%m-%d'',''now'') || '' (BREACH-DOCTOR-1 TL-R03-exclude, issue '' || CAST(?1 AS INTEGER) || '', rule '' || r.rule_key || ''): reviewed '' || r.cls || '' of tool '' || r.tool || '', a literal the owning worker or D1 emits'', a.id FROM agent_issues a JOIN breach_diagnoses d ON d.issue_id = a.id AND d.id = (SELECT MAX(x.id) FROM breach_diagnoses x WHERE x.issue_id = a.id AND x.state IN (''diagnosed'',''queued'')) JOIN r ON r.tool = json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.tool'') WHERE a.id = ?1'),
   json_array('UPDATE tool_error_exclusions SET pattern = ''TOOL-CLASSIFY-2-REVERTED '' || pattern, rationale = ''REVERTED '' || rationale WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND instr(rationale, ''TOOL-CLASSIFY-2 '') = 1 AND instr(pattern, ''TOOL-CLASSIFY-2-REVERTED '') <> 1'),
   'WITH r(rule_key, tool, pat, cls) AS (VALUES (''fg-find'', ''fleet_graph'', ''use fleet_graph_find'', ''agent-input-error''), (''gh404-issue-get'', ''github_issue_get'', ''GitHub 404: Not Found'', ''agent-input-error''), (''gh404-issue-comment'', ''github_issue_comment'', ''GitHub 404: Not Found'', ''agent-input-error''), (''gh404-git-op'', ''git_op'', ''GitHub 404: Not Found'', ''agent-input-error''), (''gh422-git-op'', ''git_op'', ''GitHub 422: No commit found for SHA'', ''agent-input-error''), (''repo-git-op'', ''git_op'', ''repo (owner/name) required'', ''agent-input-error''), (''repo-file-write'', ''github_file_write'', ''repo (owner/name) + path required'', ''agent-input-error''), (''self-fetch'', ''web_fetch'', ''self-fetch blocked'', ''correct-refusal''), (''ctr-timeout-exec'', ''shell_exec'', ''container timeout after'', ''infra-artifact''), (''ctr-timeout-ws'', ''container_workspace_exec'', ''container timeout after'', ''infra-artifact''), (''cfdocs-path'', ''cf_docs'', ''path must be a developers.cloudflare.com path'', ''agent-input-error''), (''cfdocs-page'', ''cf_docs'', ''docs page not found'', ''agent-input-error''), (''cfdocs-query'', ''cf_docs'', ''query required for mode'', ''agent-input-error''), (''netjs-json'', ''run_code_net'', '' is not valid JSON'', ''agent-input-error''), (''netjs-52x'', ''run_code_net'', ''error code: 52'', ''infra-artifact''), (''d1q-syntax'', ''ops_d1_query'', '': syntax error at offset'', ''agent-input-error''), (''d1q-token'', ''ops_d1_query'', ''D1_ERROR: unrecognized token'', ''agent-input-error''), (''d1q-terms'', ''ops_d1_query'', ''too many terms in compound SELECT'', ''agent-input-error''), (''d1w-token'', ''ops_d1_write'', ''D1_ERROR: unrecognized token'', ''agent-input-error''), (''d1w-terms'', ''ops_d1_write'', ''too many terms in compound SELECT'', ''agent-input-error'')), t AS (SELECT json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.tool'') AS tool FROM breach_diagnoses d WHERE d.issue_id = ?1 AND d.rule_id = ''TL-R03-exclude'' ORDER BY d.id DESC LIMIT 1) SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM r JOIN t ON t.tool = r.tool) THEN ''exclusion-missing'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM r JOIN t ON t.tool = r.tool WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM tool_error_exclusions x WHERE x.pattern = r.pat)) THEN ''exclusion-missing'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed', 'delegated', 4, 20, 1, 'on', 'The tool of an open tool-signal issue has unexcluded errors in the last 24 hours that a reviewed literal of that tool covers (20 reviewed classes in the rule, each a constant text its owning worker or D1 emits: input validation, a correct refusal, an infrastructure artifact). Action: INSERT OR IGNORE of that tool''s literals into tool_error_exclusions with issue_id = the case issue (the table the TOOL-FAILURE and TOOL-ERROR-RATE triggers, tool_failures_24h and the loop-breaker view read), one case per tool (the lowest open issue id), rationale TOOL-CLASSIFY-2 with the issue id. Surge guard (the filter''s alternate path): no exclusion while the excluded-class errors of the tool are 30 percent or more of at least 10 calls in 6 hours, because a real outage must not read as a class; fm-tool-exclusion-hides-outage watches it. Revert: renames the patterns this issue added (issue_id = ?1) so they match nothing; a case that only shared a literal added none and reverts none. The event text is only a haystack for instr(); it is never copied. REVIEW 2026-10-26 (shared literals): 4 of the 20 literals belong to several tools (GitHub 404: Not Found to three, container timeout after, D1_ERROR: unrecognized token and too many terms in compound SELECT to two), and tool_error_exclusions.pattern is its primary key, so the second case of a shared literal in one tick inserted nothing and failed no-rows. The trigger now defers a tool: it names a tool only when no other eligible tool (covered errors, no surge, lower lowest-issue-id) shares one of its absent literals, so the tools named in one tick insert disjoint literals and each insert changes a row whatever order the engine processes them in (priority, not id); the deferred tools follow one tick later with the literals of their own (ops_d1_query keeps its syntax-error literal when ops_d1_write took the two it shares) or need no case because the shared literal now classes their errors and TL-R03-close closes them. Verify reads the outcome and not who wrote it: every reviewed literal of the case tool is a pattern in tool_error_exclusions. Known limit: the exclusion is global by substring, so a literal added for a quiet tool also hides the same text from a tool in a surge; fm-tool-exclusion-hides-outage watches that per tool.');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO breach_playbooks (rule_id, version, family, cause_class, action_kind, trigger_sql, action_sql, revert_sql, verify_sql, min_ladder, max_per_tick, max_per_day, enabled, mode, note) VALUES
  ('TL-R05-dedupe', 1, 'TOOL-FAILURE', 'duplicate-tool-signal', 'sql', 'WITH iss AS (SELECT id, CASE WHEN title LIKE ''TOOL-FAILURE: % [error]'' THEN substr(title, 15, length(title) - 22) WHEN title LIKE ''SELF-AUDIT-TOOLERR: %'' THEN substr(title, 21) WHEN title LIKE ''[self-heal] tool % failing%'' THEN substr(title, 18, instr(substr(title, 18), '' '') - 1) WHEN title LIKE ''TOOL-ERROR-RATE-%-1'' THEN substr(title, 17, length(title) - 18) END AS tool, CASE WHEN title LIKE ''TOOL-FAILURE:%'' THEN 0 WHEN title LIKE ''SELF-AUDIT-TOOLERR:%'' THEN 1 WHEN title LIKE ''TOOL-ERROR-RATE-%'' THEN 1 ELSE 2 END AS rk FROM agent_issues WHERE status = ''open'' AND (title LIKE ''TOOL-FAILURE: %'' OR title LIKE ''SELF-AUDIT-TOOLERR: %'' OR title LIKE ''[self-heal] tool %'' OR title LIKE ''TOOL-ERROR-RATE-%-1'')), v AS (SELECT id, tool, rk FROM iss WHERE tool IS NOT NULL AND length(tool) BETWEEN 2 AND 40 AND tool NOT GLOB ''*[^a-z0-9_]*''), canon AS (SELECT tool, MIN(rk * 1000000000 + id) AS k FROM v GROUP BY tool HAVING COUNT(*) > 1) SELECT v.id AS issue_id, ''tool-signal-dup'' AS subject, json_object(''tool'', v.tool, ''canonical_issue'', c.k % 1000000000, ''open_signals'', (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM v x WHERE x.tool = v.tool)) AS facts_json FROM v JOIN canon c ON c.tool = v.tool JOIN agent_issues a ON a.id = v.id WHERE v.rk * 1000000000 + v.id > c.k AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM work_claims wc WHERE (wc.issue_id = a.id OR wc.path = ''issue:'' || a.id) AND wc.released_at IS NULL AND wc.expires_at > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now''))',
   json_array('UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = ''superseded'', last_verdict = ''superseded:closure-superseded'', last_attempt_at = datetime(''now'') WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND status IN (''active'',''holding'',''needs-machine-probe'',''probe-review-refused'')', 'INSERT INTO issue_triage (issue_id, rc, triage_state, owner, sla_due_at, close_evidence) SELECT a.id, ''breach-doctor:TL-R05-dedupe'', ''closed'', ''breach-doctor'', datetime(''now''), ''SUPERSEDED BY #'' || json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.canonical_issue'') || '': both issues report the same tool signal (tool '' || json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.tool'') || '', '' || json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.open_signals'') || '' open issues for it, TOOL-SIGNAL-ONE-PATH-1). Issue #'' || json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.canonical_issue'') || '' stays open and carries the probe on the tool error share. Closed by breach-doctor rule TL-R05-dedupe from issue ids and a count only.'' FROM agent_issues a JOIN breach_diagnoses d ON d.issue_id = a.id AND d.id = (SELECT MAX(x.id) FROM breach_diagnoses x WHERE x.issue_id = a.id AND x.state IN (''diagnosed'',''queued'')) WHERE a.id = ?1 AND a.status = ''open'' AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues s WHERE s.id = json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.canonical_issue'') AND s.status = ''open'') ON CONFLICT(issue_id) DO UPDATE SET rc = excluded.rc, triage_state = ''closed'', owner = ''breach-doctor'', close_evidence = excluded.close_evidence'),
   json_array('UPDATE issue_triage SET triage_state = ''triaged'', close_evidence = NULL WHERE issue_id = ?1', 'UPDATE agent_issues SET status = ''open'', close_channel = NULL, updated_at = CAST(strftime(''%s'',''now'') AS INTEGER) * 1000 WHERE id = ?1 AND status = ''closed''', 'UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = ''active'', last_verdict = NULL WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND status = ''superseded'' AND last_verdict = ''superseded:closure-superseded'''),
   'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE id = ?1 AND status IN (''closed'',''resolved'')) THEN ''issue-reopened'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_triage it JOIN agent_issues s ON s.id = CAST(substr(it.close_evidence, 16) AS INTEGER) WHERE it.issue_id = ?1 AND it.close_evidence LIKE ''SUPERSEDED BY #%'') THEN ''ok'' ELSE ''successor-missing'' END AS observed', 'delegated', 6, 30, 1, 'on', 'More than one open issue for one tool across the four producers of the same signal (trigger tool_error_files_issue_v2 TOOL-FAILURE, trigger tool_error_rate_filer_v3_ins TOOL-ERROR-RATE, the self-audit step SELF-AUDIT-TOOLERR, qnfo-ops telemetryAnalyze [self-heal] tool). The TOOL-FAILURE row is the survivor (else the lowest id); the others close as SUPERSEDED BY #survivor with their contracts superseded in the same atomic batch. The tool name is validated to [a-z0-9_] and never copied from text; no issue with a code-task line or a live work claim is touched (the engine skips owned issues). Live 2026-10-26: fleet_graph and github_repo_read each have a TOOL-FAILURE row and a SELF-AUDIT-TOOLERR row.');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO breach_playbooks (rule_id, version, family, cause_class, action_kind, trigger_sql, action_sql, revert_sql, verify_sql, min_ladder, max_per_tick, max_per_day, enabled, mode, note) VALUES
  ('TL-R07-secret', 1, 'SECRET-CHANGE-OBSERVED', 'secret-change-worker-in-sync', 'sql', 'WITH w AS (SELECT a.id AS issue_id, s.service AS worker, substr(a.title, -10) AS day FROM agent_issues a JOIN service_registry s ON s.kind = ''worker'' AND a.title = ''SECRET-CHANGE-OBSERVED: '' || s.service || '' '' || substr(a.title, -10) WHERE a.status = ''open'' AND a.title LIKE ''SECRET-CHANGE-OBSERVED: % ____-__-__'' AND s.service NOT GLOB ''*[^a-z0-9-]*''), c AS (SELECT w.issue_id, w.worker, MAX(e.ts) AS change_ts, MAX(CAST(json_extract(e.meta, ''$.version'') AS INTEGER)) AS ver FROM w JOIN cloud_ops_events e ON e.kind = ''secret-change'' AND substr(e.ts, 1, 10) = w.day AND json_extract(e.meta, ''$.worker'') = w.worker GROUP BY w.issue_id, w.worker) SELECT c.issue_id AS issue_id, ''secret-worker-in-sync'' AS subject, json_object(''worker'', c.worker, ''secret_version'', c.ver, ''change_age_min'', CAST((julianday(''now'') - julianday(c.change_ts)) * 1440 AS INTEGER), ''deploys_after'', (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM deployment_history h WHERE h.resource_name = c.worker AND h.status = ''success'' AND h.deployed_at > c.change_ts), ''props_restores'', (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM cloud_ops_events r WHERE r.kind = ''binding-props-restore'' AND r.ts > c.change_ts AND json_extract(r.meta, ''$.worker'') = c.worker), ''auth_errors_2h'', (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM cloud_ops_events x WHERE x.status = ''error'' AND x.ts >= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'',''-2 hours'') AND instr(COALESCE(x.meta, ''''), c.worker) > 0 AND (instr(x.meta, ''401'') > 0 OR instr(x.meta, ''403'') > 0 OR instr(lower(x.meta), ''unauthorized'') > 0 OR instr(lower(x.meta), ''key rejected'') > 0))) AS facts_json FROM c JOIN agent_issues a ON a.id = c.issue_id WHERE (julianday(''now'') - julianday(c.change_ts)) * 1440 >= 30 AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM deployment_history h WHERE h.resource_name = c.worker AND h.status = ''success'' AND h.deployed_at > c.change_ts) AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM worker_live_audit l WHERE l.worker = c.worker AND l.match = 1 AND strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'', l.probed_at) > substr(c.change_ts, 1, 19)) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cloud_ops_events x WHERE x.status = ''error'' AND x.ts >= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'',''-2 hours'') AND instr(COALESCE(x.meta, ''''), c.worker) > 0 AND (instr(x.meta, ''401'') > 0 OR instr(x.meta, ''403'') > 0 OR instr(lower(x.meta), ''unauthorized'') > 0 OR instr(lower(x.meta), ''key rejected'') > 0)) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts fc WHERE fc.issue_id = a.id AND fc.status IN (''active'',''holding'') AND COALESCE(fc.last_verdict,'''') IN (''fail'',''vacuous-probe-result'',''probe-error'',''probe-not-machine-executable'',''probe-same-account-host'')) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM work_claims wc WHERE (wc.issue_id = a.id OR wc.path = ''issue:'' || a.id) AND wc.released_at IS NULL AND wc.expires_at > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now''))',
   json_array('INSERT INTO issue_triage (issue_id, rc, triage_state, owner, sla_due_at, close_evidence) SELECT a.id, ''breach-doctor:TL-R07-secret'', ''closed'', ''breach-doctor'', datetime(''now''), ''SECRET-CHANGE worker clause checked read-only at '' || strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'') || '': worker '' || json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.worker'') || '' secret-triggered version '' || json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.secret_version'') || '' is '' || json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.change_age_min'') || '' minutes old, '' || json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.deploys_after'') || '' successful deploy(s) since, worker_live_audit reads match=1 after the change, '' || json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.props_restores'') || '' binding-props-restore event(s), '' || json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.auth_errors_2h'') || '' 401 or 403 errors naming the worker in the last 2 hours. Not measured, so not claimed: that every other consumer of the changed secret (other workers holding a copy, GitHub Actions secrets, the owner''''s clients) works with it, and that a rotated-out value is no longer accepted (no secret name or value was read and no old value was tried). One of the three clauses of the definition of done is measured here. Closed by breach-doctor rule TL-R07-secret from event, deploy and audit counts only.'' FROM agent_issues a JOIN breach_diagnoses d ON d.issue_id = a.id AND d.id = (SELECT MAX(x.id) FROM breach_diagnoses x WHERE x.issue_id = a.id AND x.state IN (''diagnosed'',''queued'')) WHERE a.id = ?1 AND a.status = ''open'' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts fc WHERE fc.issue_id = a.id AND fc.status IN (''active'',''holding'') AND COALESCE(fc.last_verdict,'''') IN (''fail'',''vacuous-probe-result'',''probe-error'',''probe-not-machine-executable'',''probe-same-account-host'')) ON CONFLICT(issue_id) DO UPDATE SET rc = excluded.rc, triage_state = ''closed'', owner = ''breach-doctor'', close_evidence = excluded.close_evidence'),
   json_array('UPDATE issue_triage SET triage_state = ''triaged'', close_evidence = NULL WHERE issue_id = ?1', 'UPDATE agent_issues SET status = ''open'', close_channel = NULL, updated_at = CAST(strftime(''%s'',''now'') AS INTEGER) * 1000 WHERE id = ?1 AND status = ''closed'''),
   'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE id = ?1 AND status IN (''closed'',''resolved'')) THEN ''ok'' ELSE ''issue-reopened'' END AS observed', 'delegated', 4, 12, 1, 'measure', 'TL-R07-secret is shipped in measure (REVIEW 2026-10-26): it records the case for each matching issue and closes none. An open SECRET-CHANGE-OBSERVED issue (category security, filed by qnfo-ops SECRET-CHANGE-WATCH-1) has a definition of done of three clauses: every consumer of each changed secret works, a rotated-out value is not re-accepted, and the evidence is in close_evidence. The rule measures one: the registered worker (name checked against service_registry, never copied from the title) has a successful deploy and a worker_live_audit match=1 after the change (30 minutes or older) and no 401 or 403 error naming it in 2 hours. Read only: no secret-lock is needed and no secret name or value is read. The action''s evidence lists the two clauses it did not measure and does not say verified. Closing on one clause of three is a decision for the owner-visible record, not for a rule: the switch is UPDATE breach_playbooks SET mode = ''on'' WHERE rule_id = ''TL-R07-secret'' by migration with its decision_log row, or a probe that measures the other two clauses (control breach-doctor-secret-change-measure, review by 2026-11-02). Live 2026-10-26: qnfo-ai-search, qnfo-fleet-dashboard, qnfo-research-exec and qnfo-ops (4 open issues; 100333 and 100418 have a binding-props-restore event); their monitoring contracts and the filing loop stay the closers.');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO breach_playbooks (rule_id, version, family, cause_class, action_kind, trigger_sql, action_sql, revert_sql, verify_sql, min_ladder, max_per_tick, max_per_day, enabled, mode, note) VALUES
  ('TL-R12-owner-dup', 1, 'OWNER-REQUEST', 'duplicate-owner-task', 'sql', 'WITH o AS (SELECT a.id AS id, p.prompt AS prompt FROM agent_issues a JOIN owner_prompts p ON p.id = substr(a.title, 12, instr(a.title, '':'') - 12) WHERE a.status = ''open'' AND a.title LIKE ''OWNER-TASK-op-%: %'' AND a.source = ''qnfo-fleet-dashboard:owner-request'' AND (p.prompt LIKE ''Fix the fleet error past its SLA:%'' OR p.prompt LIKE ''Fix FOLD-PAIR-TASK-1%'')) SELECT o.id AS issue_id, ''owner-task-dup'' AS subject, json_object(''survivor_issue'', (SELECT MIN(x.id) FROM o x WHERE x.prompt = o.prompt), ''copies'', (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM o x WHERE x.prompt = o.prompt)) AS facts_json FROM o JOIN agent_issues a ON a.id = o.id WHERE o.id > (SELECT MIN(x.id) FROM o x WHERE x.prompt = o.prompt) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM work_claims wc WHERE (wc.issue_id = a.id OR wc.path = ''issue:'' || a.id) AND wc.released_at IS NULL AND wc.expires_at > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now''))',
   json_array('UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = ''superseded'', last_verdict = ''superseded:closure-superseded'', last_attempt_at = datetime(''now'') WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND status IN (''active'',''holding'',''needs-machine-probe'',''probe-review-refused'')', 'INSERT INTO issue_triage (issue_id, rc, triage_state, owner, sla_due_at, close_evidence) SELECT a.id, ''breach-doctor:TL-R12-owner-dup'', ''closed'', ''breach-doctor'', datetime(''now''), ''SUPERSEDED BY #'' || json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.survivor_issue'') || '': both owner tasks carry the same dashboard-generated prompt (exact text match in owner_prompts, '' || json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.copies'') || '' copies). Issue #'' || json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.survivor_issue'') || '' stays open and carries the work. Closed by breach-doctor rule TL-R12-owner-dup from issue ids and an exact prompt match only.'' FROM agent_issues a JOIN breach_diagnoses d ON d.issue_id = a.id AND d.id = (SELECT MAX(x.id) FROM breach_diagnoses x WHERE x.issue_id = a.id AND x.state IN (''diagnosed'',''queued'')) WHERE a.id = ?1 AND a.status = ''open'' AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues s WHERE s.id = json_extract(d.facts_json, ''$.survivor_issue'') AND s.status = ''open'') ON CONFLICT(issue_id) DO UPDATE SET rc = excluded.rc, triage_state = ''closed'', owner = ''breach-doctor'', close_evidence = excluded.close_evidence'),
   json_array('UPDATE issue_triage SET triage_state = ''triaged'', close_evidence = NULL WHERE issue_id = ?1', 'UPDATE agent_issues SET status = ''open'', close_channel = NULL, updated_at = CAST(strftime(''%s'',''now'') AS INTEGER) * 1000 WHERE id = ?1 AND status = ''closed''', 'UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = ''active'', last_verdict = NULL WHERE issue_id = ?1 AND status = ''superseded'' AND last_verdict = ''superseded:closure-superseded'''),
   'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE id = ?1 AND status IN (''closed'',''resolved'')) THEN ''issue-reopened'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_triage it JOIN agent_issues s ON s.id = CAST(substr(it.close_evidence, 16) AS INTEGER) WHERE it.issue_id = ?1 AND it.close_evidence LIKE ''SUPERSEDED BY #%'') THEN ''ok'' ELSE ''successor-missing'' END AS observed', 'delegated', 6, 30, 1, 'on', 'Open OWNER-TASK issues (source qnfo-fleet-dashboard:owner-request) whose owner_prompts text is identical and starts with a dashboard-generated shape (Fix the fleet error past its SLA, Fix FOLD-PAIR-TASK-1): the lowest id survives, the copies close as SUPERSEDED BY #survivor. Prose the owner typed is never merged. 2026-10-26 06:00Z: 18 issues in 5 groups; the live set is 0 now (a session closed them), the rule keeps the dashboard buttons from refilling the backlog.');

-- DOCTRINE-1 (control_registry): the exclusion rule is a filter. It is not on a critical path; its reason is that 20 reviewed literals (input validation, a correct refusal, an infrastructure artifact) filed
-- the same TOOL-FAILURE issue again on every event; its alternate path is the surge guard in the trigger (no exclusion while the excluded class is 30 percent of at least 10 calls in 6 hours), the
-- unchanged view tool_failures_excluded_24h, the revert that renames the patterns, and the detector fm-tool-exclusion-hides-outage below; review by 2026-11-02.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO control_registry (control, location, kind, guards_against, critical_path, disposition, disposition_state, alternate_path, alternate_tested_at, evidence, issue_id) VALUES
 ('breach-doctor-tool-exclusion-rule', 'breach_playbooks TL-R03-exclude (reviewed literals in its trigger and action) writing qnfo-audit.tool_error_exclusions', 'filter',
  'the same caller-input, correct-refusal or infrastructure-artifact error filing a new TOOL-FAILURE issue on every event (20 reviewed literals; 31 tool-signal issues for 15 tools on 2026-10-26 06:00Z)', 0, 'keep', 'planned',
  'the surge guard in the rule (no exclusion while the excluded-class errors of a tool are 30 percent or more of at least 10 calls in 6 hours), tool_failures_excluded_24h (lists every excluded row), the revert_sql that renames the added patterns, and the detector fm-tool-exclusion-hides-outage', NULL,
  'recorded reason: docs/breach-doctor/FAMILY-TOOL-LOOP.md R3 (13 of the literals cover 108 of 162 unexcluded errors in 7 days; 20 reviewed on 2026-10-26); expiry: review by 2026-11-02 against doctor_actions_failed_24h and the surge detector; no live evidence against it', 1000266),
 ('breach-doctor-secret-change-measure', 'breach_playbooks TL-R07-secret mode = measure, read by qnfo-fleet-control breachDoctorTick()', 'hold',
  'closing a security-category SECRET-CHANGE-OBSERVED issue on one measured clause of a three-clause definition of done (consumers of the changed secret, no re-accepted rotated-out value, the evidence): the rule can show that the worker is deployed, in sync and free of 401/403 errors, not that the other two clauses hold', 0, 'keep', 'planned',
  'the rule records its would-do case for every matching issue (breach_diagnoses, mode measure) so nothing is hidden; the issues keep their monitoring contracts and the filing loop (qnfo-ops SECRET-CHANGE-WATCH-1) that closes them; the switch is UPDATE breach_playbooks SET mode = ''on'' WHERE rule_id = ''TL-R07-secret'', by migration with its decision_log row, once a recorded decision accepts the worker clause or a probe measures the other two', NULL,
  'recorded reason, review 2026-10-26 (reviewers of the tool-loop-playbooks package): the evidence the rule writes cannot show the other two clauses of the definition of done, so a rule that closes on it is a close without the measurement the issue asks for. Expiry: review by 2026-11-02, or at the first migration that adds a probe for the consumer clause, which then switches the row to on; no live evidence against the hold', 1000266);
UPDATE control_registry SET evidence = evidence || ' | BREACH-PLAYBOOKS-TOOL-LOOP-1 2026-10-26: the doctor playbook TL-R03-exclude adds reviewed rows here (rationale TOOL-CLASSIFY-2), registered as control breach-doctor-tool-exclusion-rule' WHERE control = 'tool_error_exclusions' AND instr(evidence, 'BREACH-PLAYBOOKS-TOOL-LOOP-1') = 0;
UPDATE control_registry SET location = replace(location, 'one INSERT or UPDATE on four named tables (issue_triage, agent_issues UPDATE only, remediation_contracts, issue_plans)', 'one INSERT or UPDATE on five named tables (issue_triage, agent_issues UPDATE only, remediation_contracts, issue_plans, tool_error_exclusions)'),
  evidence = evidence || ' | BREACH-PLAYBOOKS-TOOL-LOOP-1 2026-10-26: qnfo-fleet-control 0.54.0 adds tool_error_exclusions to BD_WRITE_TABLES (five tables) for the reviewed playbook TL-R03-exclude of migrations/2026-10-26-breach-playbooks-tool-loop.sql; goals and paper_learnings were asked for and refused in review (no consumer of a proposed goal); ops_config and human_actions stay off the list and the validators (a top-level id = ?1 predicate, no OR, no free-text column) are unchanged'
WHERE control = 'breach-doctor-action-allowlist' AND instr(evidence, 'BREACH-PLAYBOOKS-TOOL-LOOP-1') = 0;

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO failure_modes (fm_key, failure_mode, root_cause, remediation, detector, probe_class, first_seen, issue_id, trigger_condition, symptom, blast_radius) VALUES
 ('tool-exclusion-hides-outage', 'a reviewed tool-error exclusion hides a real outage (for example container timeout after becomes the sign of a capacity problem)',
  'tool_error_exclusions matches a literal as a substring for every event of every tool, so a class that is harmless at 2 percent is invisible at 60 percent',
  'TL-R03-exclude adds nothing while the class is 30 percent of at least 10 calls in 6 hours; fm-tool-exclusion-hides-outage reads the same numbers for the rows TOOL-CLASSIFY-2 added; the revert_sql of the case renames the patterns',
  'fm-tool-exclusion-hides-outage: no tool has 30 percent of at least 10 calls in 6 hours covered by a TOOL-CLASSIFY-2 exclusion', 'fm-tool-exclusion-hides-outage', '2026-10-26', 1000266,
  'a tool with at least 10 calls in 6 hours and 30 percent or more of them errors a TOOL-CLASSIFY-2 exclusion covers', 'tool failures stop filing issues while the tool is down', 'the tools whose class was excluded'),
 ('stale-untrusted-verdict', 'an open issue keeps the planner verdict untrusted after the trust list grew, so it has no doer for up to 7 days',
  'the planner re-reads a non-queued verdict only after PLAN_RECHECK_DAYS (7); a list edit does not re-arm it',
  'TL-R01-rearm sets planned_at to 2000-01-01 for a verdict the live list now covers; fm-stale-untrusted-verdict counts what is left',
  'fm-stale-untrusted-verdict: no untrusted verdict younger than 7 days matches the live trust list', 'fm-stale-untrusted-verdict', '2026-10-26', 1000266,
  'an untrusted issue_plans row whose source and title now match ops_config code_merge_trusted_sources', 'issues with no doer although the planner may plan them', 'every issue of a source added to the list');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO remediation_contracts (class, issue_id, verify_probe, verify_transport, max_attempts, expected_cadence_h, status, precondition, action, escalate_to, module) VALUES
 ('fm-tool-exclusion-hides-outage', NULL, 'SELECT ''0'' AS expected, CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM (SELECT e.text AS tool, COUNT(*) AS n, SUM(CASE WHEN e.status = ''error'' AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM tool_error_exclusions x WHERE instr(x.rationale, ''TOOL-CLASSIFY-2 '') = 1 AND instr(x.pattern, ''TOOL-CLASSIFY-2-REVERTED '') <> 1 AND instr(COALESCE(e.meta, ''''), x.pattern) > 0) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS classed FROM cloud_ops_events e WHERE e.kind = ''ops_ai_tool'' AND e.ts >= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'',''-6 hours'') GROUP BY e.text) WHERE n >= 10 AND classed * 100 >= 30 * n) AS TEXT) AS observed', 'd1-query', 3, 1, 'active', 'BREACH-PLAYBOOKS-TOOL-LOOP-1', 'failure-mode detector', 'qnfo-fleet-control', 'failure-mode'),
 ('fm-stale-untrusted-verdict', NULL, 'SELECT ''0'' AS expected, CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM (WITH RECURSIVE cfg(v) AS (SELECT value || '','' FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''code_merge_trusted_sources''), split(entry, rest) AS (SELECT '''', v FROM cfg UNION ALL SELECT trim(substr(rest, 1, instr(rest, '','') - 1)), substr(rest, instr(rest, '','') + 1) FROM split WHERE rest <> ''''), rules AS (SELECT CASE WHEN instr(entry, ''|'') > 0 THEN substr(entry, 1, instr(entry, ''|'') - 1) ELSE entry END AS sp, CASE WHEN instr(entry, ''|'') > 0 THEN substr(entry, instr(entry, ''|'') + 1) ELSE '''' END AS tp FROM split WHERE entry <> '''') SELECT a.id AS issue_id, ''stale-untrusted'' AS subject, json_object(''plan_age_h'', CAST((julianday(''now'') - julianday(p.planned_at)) * 24 AS INTEGER), ''planned_at_was'', p.planned_at, ''attempts'', COALESCE(p.attempts, 1)) AS facts_json FROM issue_plans p JOIN agent_issues a ON a.id = p.issue_id WHERE a.status = ''open'' AND p.outcome = ''untrusted'' AND p.planned_at > ''2001-01-01T00:00:00Z'' AND a.title NOT LIKE ''BREACH-DOCTOR-1:%'' AND p.planned_at >= strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'',''-7 days'') AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM rules r WHERE r.sp <> '''' AND r.sp <> ''*'' AND (CASE WHEN substr(r.sp, -1) = ''*'' THEN substr(COALESCE(a.source, ''''), 1, length(r.sp) - 1) = substr(r.sp, 1, length(r.sp) - 1) ELSE COALESCE(a.source, '''') = r.sp END) AND (r.tp = '''' OR substr(COALESCE(a.title, ''''), 1, length(r.tp)) = r.tp)))) AS TEXT) AS observed', 'd1-query', 3, 1, 'active', 'BREACH-PLAYBOOKS-TOOL-LOOP-1', 'failure-mode detector', 'qnfo-fleet-control', 'failure-mode');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO capability_ledger (capability, provenance, prerequisites, reliability, acquired_at, last_exercised_at, evidence) VALUES
 ('breach-doctor:tool-loop-playbooks', 'BREACH-PLAYBOOKS-TOOL-LOOP-1 (migrations/2026-10-26-breach-playbooks-tool-loop.sql, qnfo-fleet-control 0.54.0)',
  'breach doctor on (ops_config breach_doctor = on), breach_playbooks rows TL-R01, TL-R03, TL-R05, TL-R07 (measure) and TL-R12-owner-dup, BD_WRITE_TABLES with tool_error_exclusions, a planner with capacity for TL-R01', 'unmeasured until the first verified case of each rule: breaches_auto_remediated_24h', strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now'), NULL,
  'the fleet re-arms stale untrusted verdicts while the planner has capacity and verifies that the planner re-read them, classes reviewed tool errors, supersedes duplicate tool signals and duplicate owner tasks, and records observed secret changes read-only, without a session');

INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1: TD-D1Q-REJECT qnfo-ops',
  'Charter pillar: autonomy. Filed by qnfo-fleet-control BREACH-DOCTOR-1 package tool-loop-playbooks (rule TD-D1Q-REJECT) from structured facts only.' || char(10) ||
  'Facts: tool=ops_d1_query, window_min=10080, status_error=462, status_rejected=1 (ops_ai_tool events, measured 2026-10-26 11:40Z). The sibling tool ops_d1_write logged 49 rejected events in the same window.' || char(10) ||
  'Defect: d1Query returns the database error of the caller''s own SQL (a syntax error, a compound SELECT over the D1 limit, an unrecognized token, a LIKE pattern over the D1 limit, a wrong number of parameter bindings) as a plain failure, so the tool event is logged status error and counts as a tool failure. d1Write has marked the same class rejected since D1-CALLER-REJECT-1, and the event is then logged status rejected.' || char(10) ||
  'Change in qnfo-ops/worker.js d1Query: in the catch, directly after the out object is built, add a comment line D1-CALLER-REJECT-2 and one statement: if (/syntax error|SQLITE_CONSTRAINT|datatype mismatch|unrecognized token|too many terms in compound SELECT|LIKE or GLOB pattern too complex|Wrong number of parameter bindings/i.test(msg)) out.rejected = true; Leave the other branches of the catch unchanged. Bump the VERSION patch number.' || char(10) ||
  'Definition of done: the code on main holds D1-CALLER-REJECT-2 in d1Query and the canonical deploy is live, and the closing probe of this issue reads ok: an ops_d1_query event with a syntax error is logged rejected within 24 hours.' || char(10) ||
  'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-ops/worker.js' || char(10) ||
  'code-anchor: const out = { ok: false, db: bind, error: msg };' || char(10) ||
  'code-probe: {"paths":["qnfo-ops/worker.js"],"contains":"D1-CALLER-REJECT-2"}',
  'qnfo-fleet-control', 'reliability', 'medium', 'open', CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000, CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE title = 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1: TD-D1Q-REJECT qnfo-ops');

INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1: R2-PLAN-FIRST qnfo-code-orchestrator',
  'Charter pillar: autonomy. Filed by qnfo-fleet-control BREACH-DOCTOR-1 package tool-loop-playbooks (rule R2-PLAN-FIRST) from structured facts only.' || char(10) ||
  'Facts: issue_plans model calls on 2026-10-26 = 48 (code_plan_daily_cap 48, last at 01:47Z), of which 32 were re-plans of an issue that already had a verdict and 16 were first-time plans. Open dashboard owner-request issues never planned and older than 120 minutes: 8, all priority high.' || char(10) ||
  'Defect: planIssues orders its window by priority and id only, so a re-plan (a verdict older than PLAN_RECHECK_DAYS, or one re-armed by TL-R01-rearm) competes with a first-time plan of the same priority, and the daily cap of model calls is spent before the first-time plans of the high class are reached.' || char(10) ||
  'Change in qnfo-code-orchestrator/worker.js planIssues: in the const ord string, put first-time plans ahead of re-plans inside each priority class by inserting (p.issue_id IS NULL) DESC between the priority CASE and a.id, so the string reads ORDER BY CASE a.priority ... END, (p.issue_id IS NULL) DESC, a.id LIMIT. Add the comment PLAN-FIRST-TIME-FIRST-1 on the line above it. Nothing else changes: the trusted window, the cap and the gates stay as they are. Bump the VERSION patch number.' || char(10) ||
  'Definition of done: the code on main holds PLAN-FIRST-TIME-FIRST-1 and the canonical deploy is live, and the closing probe of this issue reads ok: no open dashboard owner-request issue older than 120 minutes is left without a planner verdict.' || char(10) ||
  'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-code-orchestrator/worker.js' || char(10) ||
  'code-anchor: const ord = " ORDER BY CASE a.priority WHEN ''critical'' THEN 0 WHEN ''high'' THEN 1 WHEN ''medium'' THEN 2 ELSE 3 END, a.id LIMIT ";' || char(10) ||
  'code-probe: {"paths":["qnfo-code-orchestrator/worker.js"],"contains":"PLAN-FIRST-TIME-FIRST-1"}',
  'qnfo-fleet-control', 'reliability', 'medium', 'open', CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000, CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE title = 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1: R2-PLAN-FIRST qnfo-code-orchestrator');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO remediation_contracts (class, issue_id, precondition, action, verify_probe, verify_transport, max_attempts, escalate_to, expected_cadence_h, status, module)
SELECT 'issue-' || id, id, 'born with the issue (ORPHAN-GUARD-BIRTH-1)', 'needs-machine-probe', 'needs-machine-probe', 'd1-query', 3, 'qnfo-fleet-control', 1, 'needs-machine-probe', 'birth'
FROM agent_issues WHERE title IN ('BREACH-DOCTOR-1: TD-D1Q-REJECT qnfo-ops', 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1: R2-PLAN-FIRST qnfo-code-orchestrator');

UPDATE remediation_contracts SET precondition = 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1 tool-loop-playbooks: the defect is in code the doctor cannot edit',
  action = 'the code loop edits d1Query on main, the merge lane merges it and the canonical deploy ships it, then the next caller syntax error logs status rejected',
  verify_probe = 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cloud_ops_events WHERE kind = ''ops_ai_tool'' AND text = ''ops_d1_query'' AND status = ''rejected'' AND ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'',''-24 hours'') AND instr(COALESCE(meta, ''''), ''syntax error'') > 0) THEN ''ok'' ELSE ''no ops_d1_query syntax error was logged rejected in the last 24 hours'' END AS observed',
  verify_transport = 'd1-query', max_attempts = 1000, expected_cadence_h = 1, status = 'active', module = 'breach-doctor'
WHERE class = 'issue-' || (SELECT id FROM agent_issues WHERE title = 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1: TD-D1Q-REJECT qnfo-ops' ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1);

UPDATE remediation_contracts SET precondition = 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1 tool-loop-playbooks: the defect is in code the doctor cannot edit',
  action = 'the code loop edits planIssues on main, the merge lane merges it behind the canary and the canonical deploy ships it, then the planner reaches the first-time plans first on its next day',
  verify_probe = 'SELECT ''0'' AS expected, CAST((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM agent_issues a LEFT JOIN issue_plans p ON p.issue_id = a.id WHERE a.status = ''open'' AND a.source = ''qnfo-fleet-dashboard:owner-request'' AND a.title LIKE ''OWNER-TASK-%'' AND p.issue_id IS NULL AND COALESCE(a.description, '''') NOT LIKE ''%code-task:%'' AND a.created_at < (CAST(strftime(''%s'',''now'') AS INTEGER) - 7200) * 1000) AS TEXT) AS observed',
  verify_transport = 'd1-query', max_attempts = 1000, expected_cadence_h = 1, status = 'active', module = 'breach-doctor'
WHERE class = 'issue-' || (SELECT id FROM agent_issues WHERE title = 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1: R2-PLAN-FIRST qnfo-code-orchestrator' ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1);

INSERT INTO decision_log (actor, assumption, action, evidence, outcome, blast_radius, rollback_path, capability_gain, predicted_outcome, reach_gain, surfaces_tested)
SELECT 'session_01QpQv19uh1padRwZ3u1r766',
  'the doctor engine is right to take reversible, single-issue SQL decisions from structured facts (ids, counts, enum codes); the tool, loop, secret and owner-request families need only playbook rows, one allowlist line and one engine wait (pending verify); event text is read only as an instr() haystack against reviewed constants, never copied; an effect another loop produces is verified on that effect, never on the marker the action wrote',
  'BREACH-PLAYBOOKS-TOOL-LOOP-1: six playbook rows (TL-R01-rearm, TL-R03-exclude, TL-R03-close, TL-R05-dedupe, TL-R07-secret in measure, TL-R12-owner-dup), the registry rows of the new filter and the new hold, two failure modes with detectors, and qnfo-fleet-control 0.54.0 adding tool_error_exclusions to BD_WRITE_TABLES, the pending verify and the owner-card fixes, plus two seeded code-task issues (TD-D1Q-REJECT in qnfo-ops, R2-PLAN-FIRST in qnfo-code-orchestrator). Refused in review: TL-R09-paper-route (no consumer of a proposed goal, an invented reject bar) and TL-R12-owner-card (closed at birth on live D1, no blocker_redteam row). Left out: R6 chaos (landed elsewhere), R8 cf-changelog and R10 workflow-failed (no D1 fact), R12b and R13 (no live hit, self-closing), TD-EMPTY-ERROR and R11 (no probe that can fail, no single anchor)',
  'live qnfo-audit 2026-10-26 11:40Z: 28 stale untrusted verdicts matched the trust list and the planner had made 48 of 48 model calls by 01:47Z, 32 of them re-plans, with 8 high-priority owner tasks never planned; tool issues 4 TOOL-FAILURE, 3 TOOL-ERROR-RATE, 2 SELF-AUDIT-TOOLERR for 7 tools; 4 SECRET-CHANGE-OBSERVED of workers in sync; offline suite migrations/breach-playbooks-tool-loop.test.mjs runs every rule through the real breachDoctorTick and the owner card against the live default-adopt trigger',
  'migration merged and applied by CI (migration_runs ok), qnfo-fleet-control 0.54.0 deployed through the canonical path, each rule runs in measure for 30 minutes and then acts (TL-R07-secret stays in measure)',
  'issue_plans, tool_error_exclusions, issue_triage, agent_issues (close and reopen only through the issue_triage close-sync triggers), remediation_contracts; every statement bound to one issue; per-rule caps of 1 to 6 a tick',
  'ops_config breach_doctor = off stops the engine; breach_playbooks.enabled = 0 stops one rule; every applied case stores its revert_sql in breach_diagnoses; the Rollback header disables the rows and renames the added exclusion patterns',
  'the fleet remediates the tool, loop and owner-request breach families without a session and records the secret-change family',
  'breaches_auto_remediated_24h >= 4 within 24 hours at the live hit counts of 2026-10-26 (TL-R03-exclude 1, TL-R03-close 1, TL-R05-dedupe 2), plus TL-R01 cases once the planner has a model call left (each verified only after the planner re-recorded the issue)',
  'none', 'breach_playbooks, breach_diagnoses, tool_error_exclusions, issue_plans, owner_prompts, service_registry, deployment_history, worker_live_audit; migrations/breach-playbooks-tool-loop.test.mjs; qnfo-fleet-control/breach-doctor.test.mjs'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM decision_log WHERE action LIKE 'BREACH-PLAYBOOKS-TOOL-LOOP-1%');
